{"mathcounts-potw-2026-10-12-01":[{"title":"Substitute","body":"$F(6) = 6 + 2 = 8$; $A(6) = 18 - 4 = 14$; $L(6) = 36 + 9 = 45$.\n\n**Answer: 8, 14, 45**"},{"title":"Check by relationships","body":"$A(6) = 3 \\cdot 6 - 4 = 14$ is $F(6) + 6 = 8 + 6$ ✓ (since $A(x) - F(x) = 2x - 6$). $L(6) = 6^2 + 9 = 45$.\n\n**Answer: 8, 14, 45**"}],"mathcounts-potw-2026-10-12-02":[{"title":"Combine like terms","body":"$F(x) + A(x) = (x + 2) + (3x - 4) = 4x - 2$.\n\n**Answer: $4x - 2$**"},{"title":"Check with a number","body":"At $x = 6$: $F(6) + A(6) = 8 + 14 = 22$ and $4(6) - 2 = 22$ ✓.\n\n**Answer: $4x - 2$**"}],"mathcounts-potw-2026-10-12-03":[{"title":"Inside out","body":"$L(8) = 73$; $L(73) = 5329 + 9 = 5338$; $A(5338) = 16014 - 4 = 16010$; $F(16010) = 16012$.\n\n**Answer: 16,012**"},{"title":"Compose F and A first","body":"$F(A(y)) = 3y - 4 + 2 = 3y - 2$. With $y = L(L(8)) = 73^2 + 9 = 5338$: $3(5338) - 2 = 16{,}012$.\n\n**Answer: 16,012**"}]}